{
  "requirement": "The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive, excluding leading and trailing whitespace. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no gap for either obligation. One marking question remains, and I resolved it as not a gap.\n\n**Obligations**\n1. The `requirement` string in each evidence file MUST match all Markdown inside its fenced `{req}` directive, excluding leading and trailing whitespace.\n2. Habeas MUST report changed requirement text.\n\n**Implementation**\n- **Expected text.** `collect_definitions` in `src/evidence.rs` builds the expected text. It takes `without_options(content, block.body_start..block.body_end, &blocks).trim()`, which is the whole body between the fence lines with leading and trailing whitespace removed.\n- **Body span and options.** `definition_blocks` (governed by `requirements.ci.span`) fixes the body span. `without_options` in `src/lib.rs` carries `{impl}requirements.ci.requirement_text`. It strips only the `:impl:` and `:test:` option lines from the body.\n- **Comparison and report.** `validate_evidence_file` in `src/evidence.rs` carries `{impl}requirements.ci.requirement_text`. It reads the recorded string, requires it to be a string, and compares it with `expected.text`. On a mismatch it pushes a \"`requirement text changed (source)`\" error with a diff. The diff format belongs to `requirements.ci.diagnostics`, which the same function marks.\n\n**Tests**\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` records a multi-line body that includes a fenced code example containing `{req}`. The chapter's body also ends with a newline before the closing fence, which exercises trailing-whitespace trimming. The test asserts validation has no errors.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` records \"Old text.\" against the current \"First.\" and asserts the \"requirement text changed\", \"- Old text.\" and \"+ First.\" output. This covers reporting of changed text.\n- `anchored_files_must_be_completely_covered_and_resolvable` records the body without the option lines and asserts there is no \"text changed\" error. It checks `without_options`.\n\n**Marking question**\nThe `.trim()` in `collect_definitions` is marked `{impl}` for `requirements.ci.span` and `requirements.references.anchors`, not for `requirement_text`. `requirements.ci.span` states the same trimming rule: \"Leading and trailing whitespace MUST be excluded when comparing the body with evidence\". The code is therefore marked with a requirement that specifies it. I did not treat this as a marking gap.\n\nThere is no unspecified behavior and no unacknowledged gap.",
  "references": "c0914c5fe4c4c712a6a8d74e9672f3c5fb2d82ee145425de57b43b1fd02361fc",
